 # Vision Board
 
+The board canvas uses tldraw source from `vendor/tldraw` in a Canva-inspired studio. Install the app with `npm ci`, then install the vendored repository's locked build dependencies with `cd vendor/tldraw` and `corepack yarn install --immutable --mode=skip-build`. From the project root, `npm run dev` builds the local SDK bundle and starts the app. The Fabric editor and published tldraw runtime package have been removed. Existing browser board metadata remains; old Fabric canvas records are copied on first open where supported. Tldraw's license enforcement is unchanged, so production deployment requires an appropriate license key.
+
 A private, evolving space for meaningful aspirations, small actions, and reflection.
 
-This repository contains a working Next.js application, shared validation contracts, an API package, PostgreSQL migrations, and an AWS CDK foundation. Creating a board begins with exactly two choices: Beginner mode or Reflector direct canvas. Beginner mode helps someone choose a feeling, imagine a scene, personalize a first visual piece, and see their board taking shape. They can add or revise pieces and open the full canvas when ready. Boards and notes are stored in browser localStorage; canvas data is stored in IndexedDB. This is single-browser development storage, with no account, sync, or backup yet. Authentication integration, upload endpoints, and production deployment are the next implementation milestones.
+This repository contains a working Next.js application, shared validation contracts, an API package, PostgreSQL migrations, and an AWS CDK foundation. Creating a board is one flow: choose an editable starter board, then make its placed photos and pieces your own. The studio keeps a content library beside the canvas and shows image replacement and optional meaning controls when an item is selected. You can select, move, resize, and multi-select items; use Hand or Space to pan; zoom and fit the board; optionally show an alignment grid and snap items to it; edit text; duplicate and arrange pieces; crop or mirror photos; choose a board background; adjust opacity, rotation, and text appearance; undo or redo edits within the current session; upload images; and download a PNG or JSON backup. You can also leave and remove private revisit notes from the board inspector. Boards and notes are stored in browser localStorage; canvas data is stored in IndexedDB. Backups are manual and there is no account or cloud sync yet. Authentication integration, upload endpoints, and production deployment remain future milestones.
+
+The UI uses locally owned shadcn components on Radix primitives for popovers, tooltips, switches, dialogs, and forms. Phosphor icons mark the main content categories, while Lucide icons serve utility actions.
+The visual foundations, workspace anatomy, and interaction rules are documented in [UI_SYSTEM.md](UI_SYSTEM.md). The [editor feature matrix](EDITOR_FEATURE_MATRIX.md) tracks the six-phase implementation and remaining gaps.
 
